# built
host/target/
refs/
# raw frames the host writes (each effect's video.rgb; the cut's alone is 43 MB); they rebuild from the machines
*.rgb
# renders, and videos and animations of any kind, are never kept: the repository is source; except data the
# machines are dealt
*.mp4
*.gif
!segments/polys/data/boxes.rgb
demokit/target/
# what cargo cardiac build writes beside each machine: its decks (NAME.cqb, NAME.2.cqb ...), their slots, its panic
# map, and with --emit its listings and assembly; the host loads the decks
segments/**/*.cqb
segments/**/*.cqb.meta
segments/**/*.map
segments/**/*.cq
segments/**/machines/*.asm
# cargo cardiac build's own builds of the machines
segments/target/
# the test cut's layer (segments/cut/test/make_layer.py makes it) and what the test cut and its dry run write
*.rgba
segments/cut/test/hd.txt
segments/cut/test/costs.txt
segments/cut/tally.txt
# generated data the film reads, kept packed in each segment's generated.tar.xz (build.sh unpacks it); below, each
# file's generator
# the dive's HD creatures' atlases (segments/deep/data/make_hd.py makes them)
segments/deep/data/hd_*.bin
segments/deep/data/knob.bin
segments/accel/data/traffic.bin
# the train's scene and tables (segments/train/data/make_data.py, make_tables.py)
segments/train/data/scene.bin
segments/train/data/tables.bin
# the night's scene and footage (segments/night/data/make_data.py)
segments/night/data/scene.bin
segments/night/data/clips.bin
segments/night/data/tables.bin
# the stadium party's scene and pictures (segments/stadium/data/make_data.py)
segments/stadium/data/scene.bin
segments/stadium/data/pictures.bin
segments/rooms/data/rooms.bin
segments/sqend/data/sqend.bin
# the dorm's 3D renders (made in Blender ahead of time)
segments/rooms/data/dorm3d/
__pycache__/
# the host's other cargo builds (native, PGO)
host/target-*/
# generated data, rebuilt by their make_*.py (see the segments' READMEs)
segments/train/data/tables_h.bin
# the soundtrack's mix, which the tracks are made from (made outside this repository; the player and render play the tracks)
segments/music/soundtrack.s16
# the soundtrack's tracks (packed in segments/music/generated.tar.xz)
segments/music/*.track
# the generators' Python (requirements.txt)
.venv/
